":"NYJ","distance":0.47,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"DET","distance":0.4821,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"LAC","distance":0.5367,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Shane Steichen"},{"season":2019,"team":"NYG","distance":0.5552,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"DET","distance":0.7941,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Kelvin Sheppard"},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.7966,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.8027,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"HOU","distance":0.8395,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":0.8472,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Jaguars went 1-15 in 2020 and were outscored 492 to 306. Neither side held up, as the offense ranked 28th in EPA per play and the defense 30th in EPA allowed. What set them apart was the highest pass rate and the highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Jaguars offense struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Gardner Minshew ran the passing game, with D.J. Chark leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Jaguars had one of the worst defenses in the league, ranking 25th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. Josh Hines-Allen was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Dawuane Smoot, who had 5.5 sacks despite playing only 59% of the snaps. In terms of scheme, they had the highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Jaguars were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 72% of field goals, which was one of the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 20% of the money on the books. The offense also turned over more of its roster than most, with 48% of its snaps going to players who were on the team the year before.","players":"Gardner Minshew played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 2,259 yards. Targets were spread around, with D.J. Chark and Keelan Cole leading a group where nobody took more than a fifth of the looks. James Robinson handled most of the work in the backfield with 80% of the carries. On defense, Dawuane Smoot led the team with 5.5 sacks and Joe Schobert picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2024 Giants under Brian Daboll and the 2019 Jets. Their defense looked most like the 2025 and 2023 Lions.","trends":"The offense went from 23rd in EPA per play in 2019 to 28th in 2020, a modest decline. The defense moved from 27th in EPA allowed per play in 2019 to 30th in 2020, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was two-high safety rate, which went from 16% to 84%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2020. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}